    "id": "ccmp-wind-v3-high-res",
    "stac_version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "CCMP High-Resolution experimental product provides enhanced spatial detail at 0.125° (~12.5 km) resolution for ocean surface winds. This experimental dataset uses advanced interpolation and data fusion techniques to downscale the standard 0.25° CCMP product while preserving the multi-satellite calibration and quality control of the operational system. The higher resolution is particularly valuable for coastal Southern Ocean applications, mesoscale ocean feature studies around Antarctica, and detailed air-sea flux calculations near the ice edge. While experimental, this product demonstrates improved representation of wind gradients, topographic effects on winds near Antarctic coastal regions, and finer-scale wind patterns associated with polynyas and marginal ice zones. The product maintains 6-hourly temporal resolution and includes the same wind vector components and quality flags as the standard CCMP product.",
